function paths(lane) {
  return `Your paths: LANE = ${SP}/lanes2/${lane.key} (an APFS clone of the whole integrated MAIN repo made after the round-11 integration; NOT a git worktree and not MAIN; edit freely), BASE = ${BASE} (the same snapshot, never edit it: the merge diffs LANE against it), WORK = ${SP}/work2/${lane.key} (all heavy outputs, LOG.md), your lab port = ${lane.port} (start it yourself in the background: cd LANE/retrux-web && PORT=${lane.port} nohup node hero-lab/serve.mjs > WORK/lab.log 2>&1 &; stop it before you return). MAIN = ${MAIN} (read-only for you; its lab :5173 and the Next dev server :3000 must keep running; :5173 now serves the integrated round-11 build, :5179 the round-10 baseline if running). Validators: MAIN/hero-pipeline/validate (shoot_qc.mjs, shoot_pointer.mjs, shoot_sweep.mjs, shoot_holdseq.mjs, perf_probe.mjs, region_stats.py; env LAB = your lab URL, env QS = extra query string). The earlier lanes' tools, logs and evidence are in ${SP}/work/{env,hold,ice} (and their worktrees ${SP}/lanes/{env,hold,ice}); read MAIN/notes/round11/INTEGRATION.md and handoff_*.md for the merged state and every switch. Reference: MAIN/hero-pipeline/reference (ref_F000.png, loop_F000/F015/F030/F045.png, ref_F358/F402/F420/F453/F460.png), MAIN/refs/hold_frames (F328-F472 every 4 frames), MAIN/refs/videos (Default Loop.mp4, State 2 to 5.mp4). The heavy-process gate: ${SLOT} '<lane>:<what>' -- <cmd> [args...] (light mode while the user works; never hold it while you think).`
}

